<title>CANADA: Canada's Martin extends special bank tax.</title>
<headline>Canada's Martin extends special bank tax.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The federal government plans to extend a special tax on banks until October 31, 1998, Finance Minister Paul Martin said on Tuesday as he presented his fiscal 1997 budget.</p>
<p>The capital tax surcharge on large deposit-taking institutions, introduced in the 1995 budget, is currently scheduled to expire on October 31, 1997.</p>
<p>The surcharge will continue to apply at a rate of 12 percent of capital tax, the government said.</p>
<p>((Reuters Ottawa Bureau, 613-235-6745))</p>
</text>
